    "hypothesis": "Storing strings in a packed record array and stably radix-sorting record indices by bytes should replace repeated comparisons and improve sequential memory access while preserving strcmp-compatible ordering.",
    "notes": "Uses the declared string length as the initial record width and expands safely if a token is longer. Offset and bucket-count inputs are consumed but do not constrain the global sort.",
